{"step_index":250,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T14:23:54Z","input_tokens":2859,"cache_read_tokens":205384,"output_tokens":1385,"content":"### Fixed: Uploaded Document Now Matches Digitized Parcha (Zero Fake Items)\n\nThe issue was caused by a static mock fallback in the local document extractor that injected placeholder inventory (`\"General Wholesale Inventory Batch #1\"`, `\"Retail Packaging\"`) whenever a bill was uploaded without a Gemini API key. \n\nWe have completely removed the hardcoded mock items and implemented **real client-side OCR and text extraction**, ensuring that the digitized parcha matches the actual uploaded bill.\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 What Was Fixed & Implemented\n\n#### 1. Real Client-Side OCR & Text Parsing\n- **In-Browser OCR Engine ([`index.html`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/index.html) & [`aiExtractor.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/aiExtractor.js)):**\n  - Integrated **Tesseract.js** for invoice photos/images (`.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.webp`) and **PDF.js** for PDF invoices.\n  - OCR runs **directly inside your browser** on your device, reading the actual words and numbers printed on your bill.\n- **Strict Deterministic Invoice Parser ([`utils/invoiceTextParser.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/invoiceTextParser.js)):**\n  - Extracts the **actual vendor name** from the bill header.\n  - Detects the **real 15-character GSTIN** via regex.\n  - Extracts the **actual invoice number** and **invoice date**.\n  - Parses the **actual line items** (description, quantity, rate, amount) found in the document.\n  - Extracts the declared subtotal, CGST, SGST, IGST, and grand total.\n\n#### 2. Zero-Hallucination Guarantee\n- **No More Fake Items:** The extractor will **never invent or hallucinate dummy items**.\n- If a line item rate or quantity is faint or smudged, it extracts the actual description text from the bill and marks it with an `Unclear / Blurry` badge rather than generating fictional inventory.\n- Non-invoice uploads (selfies, landscapes, chat screenshots) are caught by the gatekeeper and rejected with all financial fields left empty.\n\n#### 3. Real Document Toggle & Raw OCR Inspector ([`InvoiceViewer.js`](file:///Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/components/InvoiceViewer.js))\nWhen you upload a bill, the viewer header provides a 3-way toggle:\n1. **`📄 Digitized Parcha`:** The structured invoice view containing your document's parsed line items and real-time bounding boxes.\n2. **`📷 Original Document`:** The exact physical photo or PDF you uploaded.\n3. **`🔍 Raw OCR`:** An inspector showing the exact raw text lines detected by the OCR engine from your document.\n\n#### 4. Live Progress Indicator\n- When uploading a file, the audit modal displays real-time OCR status (e.g. *\"Reading bill text: 65%\"*).\n\n---\n\n### 🧪 Test the Fix\n\n1. Open [http://localhost:3000](http://localhost:3000) in your browser.\n2. Drag and drop or snap a photo of any real grocery, electrical, or wholesale bill.\n3. Observe the live scan progress as Tesseract reads the document text.\n4. On the review screen, switch between **`📷 Original Document`** and **`📄 Digitized Parcha`** to verify that the digitized items and numbers match your uploaded bill.\n5. Click **`🔍 Raw OCR`** to inspect the text read from the document.","thinking":"The issue stems from a hardcoded fallback in the extraction process, specifically displaying irrelevant inventory items. This fallback mechanism was triggered when the primary extraction failed, leading to incorrect data presentation. The fix involves removing the static inventory item fallback. Now the extractor should either provide a valid response or return an empty state instead of the incorrect hardcoded data.\n\n\nThe previous fix addresses the hardcoded fallback, but the application was still relying on a mock dataset when the Gemini API key was missing. The core issue lies in the absence of real document parsing when the API key is unavailable.\n\nImplemented client-side OCR using Tesseract.js and PDF.js to directly extract text from user uploads. The `invoiceTextParser.js` utility was created to parse extracted data, extracting vendor name, GSTIN, invoice details, line items, and totals. To maintain data integrity, unreadable line items are now marked instead of being fabricated. A real document viewer, with digitized invoice, original document, and raw OCR inspection views, was also added.\n\n\n"}
