{"step_index":252,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-02T16:28:43Z","input_tokens":209931,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":2219,"thinking":"The request emphasizes handling incomplete or ambiguous invoice data. Need to identify missing or unclear invoice details. If such issues are detected, the process will halt, requesting valid user input before proceeding with calculations. This initial understanding guides the approach to assess and handle document imperfections.\n\n\nCritical fields like vendor name, invoice number, and date are necessary for processing; also halt calculations for line items with unclear rates. Current behavior flags issues but proceeds with calculations, while the desired state blocks the process with an \"Input Required\" prompt until missing or unclear data is provided. This will halt generation of final results until validation is complete.\n\n\nIdentifying specific conditions for halting processing. Incomplete or ambiguous data categories include unclear line item details, missing critical header fields (invoice number, date, vendor, declared total), and invalid GSTINs. The criteria involve checking for blurriness, zero/negative values in line items, and missing/invalid values in key header fields using predefined rules and regular expressions. If these conditions are met, the processing will be paused and user input will be required.\n\n\nThe user interface needs to present a clear form alongside the original document image. This form should prompt for missing or unclear details with input fields for specific data like rates, GSTINs, and invoice numbers. Calculations will be locked until valid input is provided, ensuring accuracy. Testing should encompass scenarios with complete, incorrect, and incomplete data to validate the new halt-and-prompt behavior. For instance, an invoice with a missing GSTIN and blurry rate should trigger the input prompts.\n\n\nThe `checkMissingOrUnclearInputs` function within the audit engine analyzes invoice data, returning a flag and a list of missing fields. If incomplete data exists and user confirmation is pending, the process sets the status to \"INPUT_REQUIRED,\" preventing further calculations until valid inputs are confirmed. The \"Input Required\" state triggers an interactive prompt displaying missing fields with input boxes and a confirmation button, replacing the standard scorecard.\n\n\nThe \"Input Required\" state now triggers a refined user interface. The UI presents a clear form alongside the original document. The form includes specific input fields for missing or unclear invoice details. These include fields for line item details, GSTIN, invoice number, date, and declared total, with visual prompts and alerts. Upon user submission, the `invoice.user_confirmed_inputs` flag is set and invalid flags are cleared to allow calculation to continue.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"read_file","args":{"EndLine":"75","Path":"\"/Users/pranit405/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/audit-it/utils/auditEngine.js\"","StartLine":"35"}}]}
